Command:
Get-CimInstance Win32_PhysicalMemory | Format-Table DeviceLocator, Speed, @{Name="Capacity (GB)"; Expression={$_.Capacity / 1GB}}
Response:
DeviceLocator Speed Capacity (GB)
------------- ----- -------------
DIMM 0         5600            16
Explanation: Here, CimInstance retrieves information about physical memory (RAM) from Win32_PhysicalMemory, that stores data about memory.
Response displays data regarding device locator (memory module address that is labeled as DIMM 0, that is the same thing as Slot 1),
module speed of 5600 MT/s (Mega Transfers per second), and memory capacity (how much data can be stored in real time during running) of 16 gigabytes (GB) 


